@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Chromium AROS recording through AHI
+
+Status: hypothesis
+
+## Rationale
+
+The AROS AudioManager currently has playback only and fake input streams.
+Enumerate AHI recording modes and open the selected mode through AHI_NO_UNIT,
+independently of the configured playback unit. Recording, message ports and
+control lifetime belong to a worker task. Stop joins it after AHI recording
+is stopped and its audio control released.
+
+The hook is an integer-only producer into a bounded single-producer,
+single-consumer buffer. It cannot allocate, lock, log, call Chromium, or alter
+unpreserved SIMD registers. The consumer converts signed native 8/16/32-bit
+mono/stereo PCM to AudioBus float channels. Overflow drops the incoming block
+and reports dropped duration. A rate mismatch or stalled recording reports
+an error instead of relabeling samples or synthesizing silence.
+
+## Baseline and validation
+
+Draft uses Chromium 154e4ec5e2af5ada8866c0bdf903edd899a206fd; Claude's integration
+baseline/build confirmation is pending. Both AHI input and AudioManager objects
+cross-compile with the current CEF command into private outputs. Disassembly
+confirms no SIMD registers in the recording hook. Standalone ASan/UBSan tests
+pass conversion, partial reads, wrap, overflow and 100000 concurrent frames.
+The driver-side USB mic was previously tested on AROS; this new Chromium stream
+still needs native runtime, stop/reopen and combined-camera verification.
+
+Evidence: /run/media/terminills/Codex/adt-uvc-01a15bd6/evidence/chromium-capture-draft
+Relay: JOB-0212 (parent JOB-0066)
